    ['type' => 'p', 'html' => 'For example, a logistics company may need a centralized platform that connects order management, delivery tracking, inventory records, and customer notifications. If separate tools cannot communicate properly, a tailored solution may reduce duplication and improve visibility. See how this worked in our <a href="custom-software-development-logistics-business-case-study">custom software development logistics case study</a>.'],
    ['type' => 'p', 'html' => 'The decision should depend on your requirements, available budget, integration needs, and expected growth—not simply on which option has more features. For a deeper comparison, read <a href="why-custom-software-development-is-essential-for-business-growth-in-2026">why custom software development is essential for business growth</a>.'],

    ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => '3. Evaluate the Total Cost, Not Just the Initial Price'],
