    ['type' => 'p', 'html' => 'A low-cost solution may become expensive if employees need to perform additional manual tasks or if it cannot integrate with existing systems.'],
    ['type' => 'p', 'html' => 'Before making a decision, estimate the total cost of ownership over the next three to five years. Compare that estimate with the potential benefits, such as reduced administrative work, fewer errors, faster processing, and improved customer service.'],
    ['type' => 'p', 'html' => 'For instance, if automation saves several employee hours each week, calculate the value of that recovered time. This gives you a more realistic basis for evaluating the investment. Ongoing costs matter too: learn how to <a href="reduce-software-maintenance-costs">reduce software maintenance costs</a> and <a href="software-project-budget-management">why software projects go over budget</a>.'],

    ['type' => 'h2', 'text' => '4. Check Integration With Your Existing Systems'],
